# O-021 decided 2026-09-09 (option 2): the Brain is tracked by default.
# Only genuinely local things stay ignored: the personal daily log, vendored
# external tools, tool state, owner-supplied external inputs, and the two
# September audits below. Those two contain a working step-by-step
# reproduction of U-022 -- fine in a private repo, not in a public one -- and
# stay ignored until O-019 lands, per the owner's standing call. Secrets scan
# 2026-09-09 found no keys/tokens/private keys anywhere in the Brain, but
# staging/committing remains a separate owner decision: this edit only makes
# files trackable, it tracks nothing.
/_SCOUTIT_BRAIN/00_DAILY_LOG/
/_SCOUTIT_BRAIN/12_EXTERNAL_TOOLS/
/_SCOUTIT_BRAIN/.impeccable/
/_SCOUTIT_BRAIN/13_EXTERNAL_INPUTS/
/_SCOUTIT_BRAIN/08_OPERATIONS_AND_BACKLOG/ACTION/INBOX/2026-09-01_FULL_STACK_GAP_AUDIT.md
/_SCOUTIT_BRAIN/08_OPERATIONS_AND_BACKLOG/ACTION/INBOX/2026-09-03_FULL_STACK_GAP_AUDIT.md

# FUSE artifacts left by in-place edits over a mounted filesystem.
# Not source; they are stale open handles to replaced files.
.fuse_hidden*

# A-089, 2026-09-09 triage. Lab clutter at the repo root is local experiment
# material, not review content: manifesto cinematic lookdev, one-off transition
# runner, dev-server log. Ignored with reason recorded here; files stay on disk.
# Migrations 20260831*/20260904*/20260905* + DONE/2026-09 + A-083/A-085 plans
# are trackable (not ignored) — content unchanged. Staging/committing them is a
# separate owner decision; this edit only makes lab noise ignorable.
# CRLF: .gitattributes already enforces LF (* text=auto eol=lf). The 60+ file
# warnings are expected normalization noise until the owner approves the
# one-time `git add --renormalize .` commit named in .gitattributes.
/manifesto-lab/
/apply-transitions.mjs
/lab-server.log
# Tool-cache churn is not review content. The already-tracked
# mission-control/.impeccable/hook.cache.json keeps showing modified until the
# owner approves `git rm --cached` for it; ignore future cache copies only.
**/.impeccable/hook.cache.json
